{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": [
    "htcondor",
    "htcondordb",
    "job-metrics"
  ],
  "title": "HTCondorDB Job Resource Usage",
  "uid": "htcondordb-job-metrics",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "description": "Resource usage of running jobs, sampled from job_queue.log into the job_metrics archive (HTCONDORDB_JOB_METRICS). Requires schedd sync with job metrics enabled.",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "refresh": 1,
        "hide": 0,
        "current": {}
      },
      {
        "name": "owner",
        "label": "Owner",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "SELECT DISTINCT Owner FROM job_metrics",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "CPU cores used, by owner",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Average cores consumed per sampled job, from the change in RemoteUserCpu+RemoteSysCpu between consecutive observations. Gaps are real: a rate is undefined (never zero) when there is no usable predecessor -- a run's first samples, or an interval spanning a run boundary, where the counters restart.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "builder",
          "table": "job_metrics",
          "metrics": [
            {
              "func": "AVG",
              "attr": "CpuUtil"
            }
          ],
          "format": "timeseries",
          "timeField": "SampleTime",
          "groupBy": [
            "Owner"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Memory high-water mark, by owner",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "PEAK memory ever used, not current usage: HTCondor's MemoryUsage only ratchets up. Filtered to RunInstanceID == 0 because the shadow SEEDS this from the previous run, so for a rerun it is the maximum over all of the job's runs wearing this run's timestamp. Read it as 'how much has this job ever needed', which is the right-sizing question.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "decmbytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "builder",
          "table": "job_metrics",
          "metrics": [
            {
              "func": "MAX",
              "attr": "MemoryUsage"
            }
          ],
          "format": "timeseries",
          "timeField": "SampleTime",
          "groupBy": [
            "Owner"
          ],
          "filters": [
            {
              "attr": "RunInstanceID",
              "op": "==",
              "value": "0"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Disk I/O rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Bytes/s read and written per sampled job, differentiated at ingest from the cumulative block counters. Only populated where the procd reports block I/O.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "builder",
          "table": "job_metrics",
          "metrics": [
            {
              "func": "AVG",
              "attr": "BlockReadRate"
            },
            {
              "func": "AVG",
              "attr": "BlockWriteRate"
            }
          ],
          "format": "timeseries",
          "timeField": "SampleTime"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Memory actually used, as a fraction of what was requested",
      "type": "barchart",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The right-sizing panel, and the one that pays for this table: who asks for 64 GB and uses 4. MemUtil is MemoryUsage/RequestMemory, computed at ingest so the units are known to agree (both MiB). Restricted to first runs -- see the memory panel.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "builder",
          "table": "job_metrics",
          "metrics": [
            {
              "func": "AVG",
              "attr": "MemUtil"
            }
          ],
          "format": "table",
          "timeField": "SampleTime",
          "groupBy": [
            "Owner"
          ],
          "orderBy": "AVG(MemUtil)",
          "orderDesc": false,
          "filters": [
            {
              "attr": "RunInstanceID",
              "op": "==",
              "value": "0"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Samples by trigger",
      "type": "piechart",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "What caused each observation. Sampling is event-driven, so the 900s periodic timer is a floor: state changes, checkpoints and run endpoints add points on their own. A large 'chirp' share means jobs are publishing their own metrics frequently.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "builder",
          "table": "job_metrics",
          "metrics": [
            {
              "func": "COUNT",
              "attr": "*"
            }
          ],
          "format": "table",
          "timeField": "SampleTime",
          "groupBy": [
            "SampleTrigger"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Jobs with the largest peak memory",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The jobs behind the right-sizing numbers, so an admin can go and look at one. $__timeFilter expands to the dashboard's range over SampleTime, which the archive zone-maps -- so the range prunes whole segments instead of scanning the table.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "bbockelm-htcondordb-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawSql": "SELECT ClusterId, ProcId, Owner, MAX(MemoryUsage) AS PeakMemoryMB, MAX(RequestMemory) AS RequestedMB, MAX(MemUtil) AS Fraction FROM job_metrics WHERE $__timeFilter(SampleTime) && RunInstanceID == 0 GROUP BY ClusterId, ProcId, Owner ORDER BY MAX(MemoryUsage) DESC LIMIT 25"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
